.TH PORTOP 1 "October 2026" "portop" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
portop \- monitor TCP and UDP ports and their owning processes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B portop
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ filter ... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B portop
displays sockets, processes, systemd services and Docker containers in an
interactive terminal table. The optional filter matches ports, process names
or process identifiers. On Linux, socket and process information is read
from procfs. Visibility and permission to send signals depend on the user
running the program.
.PP
No background service is installed or started. The web dashboard starts
only when explicitly requested.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-help
Display usage and available options.
.TP
.B \-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-listen
Show only sockets in the LISTEN state.
.TP
.B \-json
Write a JSON snapshot and exit.
.TP
.BI \-interval " duration"
Set the terminal refresh interval, for example 500ms or 2s. Default: 2s.
.TP
.B \-no-dns
Disable reverse DNS resolution.
.TP
.B \-no-systemd
Disable association with systemd units.
.TP
.B \-no-docker
Disable association with Docker containers.
.TP
.B \-watch-new
Send desktop notifications when new listening ports appear, if
.BR notify-send (1)
is available.
.TP
.B \-save-baseline
Save the current listening ports to the baseline file and exit.
.TP
.B \-diff
Compare current listening ports with the saved baseline and exit.
.TP
.BI \-baseline-path " file"
Override the baseline file location.
.TP
.BI \-compose " directory"
Audit published ports in a Docker Compose project and exit. Can be
combined with
.BR \-json .
.TP
.BI \-config " file"
Read settings from the specified YAML file.
.TP
.B \-init-config
Write a commented configuration template and exit.
.TP
.B \-web
Serve the browser dashboard. Default address: 127.0.0.1:8088.
.TP
.BI \-web-port " port"
Set the loopback dashboard port.
.TP
.BI \-web-addr " address:port"
Set the dashboard listen address. Listening beyond loopback requires
.BR \-web-auth .
.TP
.B \-web-auth
Require sign-in. Without a supplied password, generate one and print it
on startup. Sessions are discarded when the program exits.
.TP
.BI \-web-user " name"
Set the sign-in username; implies authentication. Default: portop.
.TP
.BI \-web-password " password"
Set the sign-in password; implies authentication. Prefer the
PORTOP_WEB_PASSWORD environment variable to avoid exposing it in command
line arguments.
.TP
.BI \-web-tls-cert " file"
Serve HTTPS with the specified PEM certificate. Requires
.BR \-web-tls-key .
.TP
.BI \-web-tls-key " file"
PEM private key for the HTTPS certificate.
.TP
.BI \-inspect-pid " pid"
Write process details as JSON and exit.
.TP
.BI \-signal-pid " pid"
Signal a process after validating its identity. Requires
.BR \-expected-start .
.TP
.BI \-expected-start " value"
Expected process start time from
.BR \-inspect-pid .
.TP
.B \-force
Use SIGKILL instead of SIGTERM with
.BR \-signal-pid .
.PP
Options also accept two leading hyphens.
.SH KEYS
Arrow keys move the selection; Enter opens process details;
.B f
or / filters;
.B s
changes sorting;
.B e
toggles established sockets;
.B v
cycles IP versions;
.B r
refreshes;
.B c
copies the selected entry;
.B o
opens its local URL;
.B n
clears new-port marks;
.B ,
opens settings;
.B ?
opens help; and
.B q
quits.
.PP
.B k
opens the signal confirmation dialog. Then
.B y
sends SIGTERM and
.B f
sends SIGKILL. Another key cancels. Key bindings can be changed in settings.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/portop/config.yml
Optional configuration. Defaults to ~/.config/portop/config.yml.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/portop/baseline.json
Default baseline location. Defaults to ~/.config/portop/baseline.json.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for per-user configuration.
.TP
.B PORTOP_WEB_PASSWORD
Dashboard password, used when no password option is supplied.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
indicates success.
.B 1
indicates an operational error or invalid configuration.
.B 2
indicates invalid command line options.
.B 3
indicates added or removed listening ports in diff mode, or unused or
conflicting published ports in a Compose audit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
portop
portop 8080 --json --no-dns
portop --save-baseline
portop --diff --json
portop --compose /path/to/project
portop --web --web-auth
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ss (8),
.BR proc (5),
.BR kill (1)
